118
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:14,000
So I had this question from a listener who asked to

119
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
remain anonymous.

120
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,000
They said: how do you deal with scouts who are

121
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
openly disrespectful to their parents, who are

122
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:25,000
volunteering as scouters, like the scoutmaster

123
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
or assistant scoutmaster,

124
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
And they're disrespectful at meetings and camps

125
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:31,000
and other outings?

126
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
This is not following the scout law and it makes

127
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
everyone around them uncomfortable.

128
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Is this something the patrol leaders council should

129
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,000
discuss and address, or should only the

130
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
scoutmaster address this? but that has happened

131
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
and that doesn't seem to be working.

132
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Should there be consequences and, if so,

133
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
who would decide them?

134
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
It seems like a big responsibility for youth

135
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
leaders to take on.

136
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Well, that is quite a question,

137
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
and the answer isn't about who handles this

138
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
and how.

139
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
You're looking for procedural or logistic

140
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:07,000
answers to a question that's really about roles

141
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,000
and relationships.

142
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Now, this makes it a little complex,

143
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
but it's not too hard to understand.

144
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,000
We have to examine first what's going on.

145
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:20,000
A volunteer scouter is a parent and has two

146
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
roles and relationships if they have a child

147
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
involved with the unit that they're

148
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
volunteering for

149
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
And they can't occupy both of those roles

150
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
and relationships at once.

151
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:35,000
A scout and a child also has two roles

152
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:38,000
and relationships if their parent is a

153
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
volunteer scouter.

154
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
The scout and the child, they can't occupy

155
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
both those roles at once.

156
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
We should add that there is a power

157
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
differential to consider too.

158
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:51,000
A parent has more power over their child

159
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,000
than a scouter has over their scout.

160
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
You can't use parent power in your

161
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
scouting relationship-

162
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
No fair.

163
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,000
And you can't use child power in your

164
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
scouting relationship either,

165
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Because there's also the idea that a child

166
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
can push a parent's buttons more

167
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
effectively than they can provoke a

168
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,000
scouter, right,

169
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
And that's why I say there's child power

170
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,000
too.

171
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Obviously, parent power stronger than

172
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,000
scouter power, child power stronger,

173
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
stronger than scout power.

174
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
And it's all about those relationships.

175
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,000
The problems start when the two

176
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:32,000
different relationships are allowed to

177
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,000
overlap.

178
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,000
If mom is the scout master and the

179
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,000
child is a scout, the child can likely

180
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
only sees mom right,

181
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
And really not the scout master.

182
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
And vice versa for mom,

183
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Mom only sees her child and not the

184
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
scout. if you understand what I'm

185
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,000
saying,

186
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,000
If one or the other or both of those

187
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
relationships is strained, right,

188
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
If things are a little strained at

189
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
home between the parent and the child,

190
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
or things are a little strained at

191
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
scouts, between the scouter and the

192
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
scout, it's not really likely that

193
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
you're going to be very objective when

194
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
you try and switch roles.

195
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Now the responsibility principally lies

196
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
with the adult in this equation

197
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Who we hope has more mature character

198
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
tools to handle the situation.

199
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
So that explains the relationships

200
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
and the different things that bear on

201
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
them.

202
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
So let's talk about how this works

203
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,000
practically.

204
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
If you draw a line between the roles

205
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
of parent and scouter and of child

206
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,000
and scout and you make that line

207
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
the threshold of the meeting place

208
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
or the gateway of the campsite,

209
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
and you and your child have a mutual

210
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
agreement that the role changes

211
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,000
at that line, right?

212
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,000
So you define the difference between

213
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
the roles and how a parent and

214
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
child interact in one set of roles

215
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,000
and how a scout and a scouter

216
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
interact in another.

217
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Since objectivity and the power

218
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
differential is always going to be

219
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
an issue in these situations,

220
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
the child of a volunteer

221
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
scouter should be encouraged to

222
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
make a free choice of a neutral

223
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
adult involved with scouting

224
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
to resolve any issues that might

225
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
come up.

226
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Let's go back to my example again.

227
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
My mom's a scout master who is

228
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
subtly leveraging her parent

229
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
power and letting it overlap

230
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
with scouts, or that the child

231
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
is a scout and is

232
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
doing the same thing- kind of

233
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
leveraging the child power, right?

234
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
That neutral adult makes a judgment

235
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
and defines a resolution

236
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
and a lot of- and not nine out

237
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
of ten times- that resolution

238
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,000
is just going to be okay, guys,

239
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
you're mixing up the relationships.

240
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
You got to stop being that way.

241
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
come up with a hundred ways to define

242
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
being that way, right,

243
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
But you get the idea.

244
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
If either of them- either the parent

245
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
or the child- can't or won't stop

246
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
confusing these roles or making

247
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
a difficult situation, they really

248
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
just can't be a part of what's

249
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,000
happening in scouts, because we have

250
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
an oath and a law that defines our conduct

251
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
and our character, and if you can't follow

252
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,000
that, whether you're an adult

253
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,000
or a child, hey, we got a problem

254
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
and you're just not going to be able to participate.

255
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Now this is all really simple.

256
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,000
It talks really easy, right.

257
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
If a parent

258
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,000
or a child scouts conduct

259
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
is not in line with the oath and law,

260
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
they simply can't be part of what's going on.

261
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
So we don't want to try to write rules

262
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
or standard consequences.

263
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
We don't want to give this to the youth leaders,

